      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ravalli County stretches about 100 miles north‑south through the Bitterroot Valley, a long, narrow slice of southwestern Montana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roamingmontana.com/ravalli-county/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ravalli County sits in the Bitterroot Valley, bordered by the Bitterroot and Sapphire mountain ranges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roamingmontana.com/ravalli-county/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Ravalli hosted the Pablo‑Allard herd, the largest bison collection left in the United States.",
